// Permit Read only when the requesting principal is on the provider's
// allowlist, as decided by the `Access::Allowed` information provider
// (implemented in allowed.rhai).
//
// The novel shape here is the *argument*: the provider is passed
// `principal.id` — an attribute path rooted at `principal`, not `context`.
// Provider arguments are resolved pre-Cedar against the request event, and
// `principal` / `resource` roots resolve to the request scope entity (a
// trailing `.id` / `.type` projects the entity's id / type). This is the
// the temporal-logic argument rule (context / principal / resource paths + literals +
// sets); before the provider-path unification only `context.<field>` paths
// were accepted.
//
// `Access::Allowed(principal.id).allowed == true` — the provider returns
// `{ allowed: bool }`; `alice` is allowlisted, `mallory` is not.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when guardrails {
    Access::Allowed(principal.id).allowed == true
};
